===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Conquered; overpowered; crushed; submissive.
#: {{ux|en|He is '''subdued''' after the disagreement last night.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=William Shakespeare|authorlink=William Shakespeare|chapter=[[w:Othello|The Tragedie of Othello, the Moore of Venice]]|title=[[w:First Folio|Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies: Published According to the True Originall Copies]]|location=London|publisher=Printed by [[w:William Jaggard|Isaac Iaggard]], and [[w:Edward Blount|Ed[ward] Blount]]|year=1603|year_published=1623|section=Act V, scene ii|page=338|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=uNtBAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA338|oclc=606515358|passage=I pray you in your Letters, / When you ſhall theſe vnluckie deeds relate, / Speake of me, as I am. {{...}} / Of one, whoſe '''ſubdu'd''' Eyes, / Albeit un-vsed to the melting moode, / Drops teares as faſt as the Arabian Trees / Their Medicinable gumme.}}
# Not glaring in color; soft and light in tone.
#: {{ux|en|The colour scheme used for this room is '''subdued'''.}}

